this is the same class as the v1.4.3-rc.1 P1 that condition 3(a) declares cured only for diagnose-output-hook.py. The scrub list appears to have been carried unchanged by the move (I cannot diff it against base text from this tree), so this is not a regression introduced by the delta. It is also not among the cases this payload's conditions name. It may already sit in the carried debt of conditions 1 and 2, which I could not enumerate from here.\n- Minimal fix: before applying the per-entry overrides, pop from base_env the same tuple as diagnose-output-hook.py:27-34 (_CHILD_LOCATION_CARRIERS). Pin its parity with _lib/test_isolation.py in a test, as diagnose-output-hook.py already does.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/snapshot_core.py, the _write_snapshot docstring (around lines 334-341) versus :424-425.\n- The docstring says the blob \"is handed to store.set as a str on BOTH paths so the store's redact_secrets pass actually runs\". The same function hands store.set BYTES whenever _lib.redact imports, after its own field-level redaction (rail round-8). It falls back to str only when the redactor is unavailable.\n- The facade's module docstring repeats the stale claim (check_precompact_continuity.py:57-63).\n- Secrets are still redacted, but the comment names the wrong layer, which misleads anyone who audits the redaction path.\n- Fix: rewrite both docstrings to describe field-level redaction plus the bytes route, with str as the fallback.\n\nP2-2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/__init__.py:16.\n- Running exec on each part's source in the facade namespace also runs each part's docstring assignment. At runtime, check_precompact_continuity.__doc__ ends up as runtime.py's one-liner \"PreCompact hook dispatch and command-line entry point.\" instead of the ADR-153 contract text.\n- I found no runtime consumer, so this is cosmetic, but it sits under a CHANGELOG line that says entry points keep their observable contracts.\n- Fix: save namespace.get(\"__doc__\") before the loop and restore it afterwards.\n\nP2-3 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_precompact_parts/snapshot_core.py:53-79 (_resolve_project_root).\n- The function walks up to the nearest ancestor that contains .claude/ and ignores CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR. Every Claude Code machine has ~/.claude, so a hook-input cwd under $HOME but outside any project (for example a directory added with --add-dir) resolves the \"project root\" to $HOME.\n- Effects in that case: plan, ceremony and ledger lookups run against ~/.claude/plans and git runs in $HOME. When CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS is set, the hysteresis marker is written under ~/.claude/state.\n- The git-toplevel fallback also uses a fixed 2.0 s timeout outside the TIME_BUDGET_S deadline that gate() computes beforehand.\n- Impact is low (advisory hook, edge-case cwd), and the code may predate this delta.\n- Fix: when cwd is inside CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, prefer it; stop the walk-up before $HOME; pass the remaining budget to the fallback _git call.","decision":"GO","sentence":"This payload's moved code binds and resolves correctly, keeps its fail-open direction, ships to adopters, and contradicts none of the declared conditions. The only P1, the profiler's isolation missing CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, appears to predate the move and goes to the annex rather than blocking."}}}
